# Beat for demo step "Hidden bits": the answer riding home (spec 0396).
#
# The companion to beats/smuggle. That beat decoded "whoami" out of a
# captured *response*; this one is the matching *request*, carrying Bob's
# answer "experiment" through the same padded-varint channel. A single
# step: the mechanism is already understood, so this just shows the
# decryption. Advance (to quit) with space or Enter.
#
# Step text is written for a 120-column line (spec 0400).
#
# Invocation (from grehack2026.sh), on the matching request capture:
#   protolens --descriptor-set life.desc capture/NNNNNN-request.pb \
#       --script beats/smuggle2

title: The answer rides home

steps:
  - text: |
      The matching request, carrying the answer the same way: one
      hidden bit per cell, read across the grid, grouped into bytes.

        01100101 01111000 01110000 01100101 01110010
           e        x        p        e        r
        01101001 01101101 01100101 01101110 01110100
           i        m        e        n        t      → experiment

      Eve asked "whoami" in the response; Bob's machine answered
      "experiment" in the request. Neither touched the decoded Life game.

      👋 Type `:q` to quit protolens.
    node: /
